------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dataset & Textual Provenance Notice (IChingData.js)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
All English translations of the Zhouyi (the 64 Judgments / Guàcí, the 64 Great
Images / Dà Xiàng, and the 386 Line Texts / Yáocí) and all accompanying
commentaries (Judgment, Image, Structural, Nuclear, and Operative Line Counsel)
bundled in `IChingData.js` are original British-English translations and
scholarly syntheses authored by Matthew Hudson, derived directly from:

1. Public-domain Classical Chinese primary texts: the Western Zhou core text
   (Zhōuyì, 周易) and the Confucian Ten Wings (Shí Yì, 十翼: Tuàn Zhuàn,
   Dà Xiàng, Xiǎo Xiàng, Wényán Zhuàn, and Xìcí Zhuàn), alongside Song Dynasty
   commentaries by Cheng Yi (1099 CE) and Zhu Xi (1177 / 1186 CE).
2. Pre-1929 public-domain European sinological scholarship: James Legge's
   1882/1899 Oxford translation ("The Yi King", Sacred Books of the East,
   Vol. XVI) and Richard Wilhelm's 1923 German edition ("I Ging: Das Buch der
   Wandlungen", Eugen Diederichs Verlag, Jena, 1923; in the public domain
   worldwide following the author's death in 1930).

No third-party copyrighted translation text (such as Cary F. Baynes's 1950/1967
English rendering) is included in this repository. The entire codebase and the
bundled `IChingData.js` dataset are licensed under the MIT License above.
